+// OrchestrAI: numeric ranges such as `20~25℃` or `5~10%` are common in Chinese prose and web
+// evidence. Two of them in one paragraph were paired into strikethrough/subscript. A tilde
+// between a number (optionally followed by a unit sign) and another number is a range.
+const RANGE_TILDE_REGEX = /(?<=\d[°℃℉%]?)~(?=[ \t]?[-−+]?\d)/g;
+
